2,Melanau Traditional Music - YouTubeWAK Sibu 2026 opens with Melanau cultural tributeMelanau language - Detailed PediaSibu sets Malaysia record with 18.3m Melanau swing at ...AJLM promotes Melanau culture and heritage - Sarawak TribuneAustronesian Soundscapes: Performing Arts in Oceania and ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=_KbqsCXGJWM,"Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube. The third edition of the WAK Sibu Festival 2026 was officially launched on Friday evening at the Sibu Heritage Centre, this time celebrating the traditions of the Melanau people through a showcase of traditional dance and music. Melanau is an Austronesian language spoken in the coastal area of the Rajang delta on northwest Borneo, Sarawak, Malaysia and Brunei. There are several dialects—Mukah-Oya, Balingian, Bruit, Dalat, Lawas, Igan, Sarikei, Segahan, Prehan, Segalang, and Siteng. Jul 13, 2025 · SIBU: The Sibu Municipal Council (SMC) has secured a spot in the Malaysia Book of Records (MBOR) with its towering 18.3-metre Melanau swing, known as the itut. Built as the centrepiece of this year’s Borneo Cultural Festival (BCF), the swing became a major attraction, drawing 2,288 visitors, surpassing the initial target of 2,000. Jan 28, 2024 · SIBU: The Anugerah Juara Lagu Melanau (AJLM) serves as a platform to develop and dignify Melanau culture. Austronesian Soundscapes is a collection of essays on Austronesian musics that transcends disciplinary frontiers in the humanities and social sciences. In all of Austronesia, music plays a crucial role in the negotiation of cultural identities; yet research on the diversity of the Austronesian cultural belt's music has hitherto been rather sparse.","Melanau, Sibu",Austronesian
